<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41056" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕ-mollio</span></b> , no <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.</i>, ītum,
			4, v. a., <i>to make soft
			again</i>, <i>to make soft</i>, <i>soften</i> (<b>poet.</b> and in post-Aug.
			prose). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terram,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					2, 11, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">grana umore remollita,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Herb. 3, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quare ... Salmacis enervet tactosque remolliat
					artus,</span>”
				<i>softens</i>, <i>weakens</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					4, 286</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">eo se inhibitum ac remolitum, quo minus, ut
					destinarat, etc.,</span>”
				<i>softened</i>, <i>mollified</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Aug. 79</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
